# ============================================================
#  Momentum demo  -  "Crypto you can change"
#  Run:   rm -rf data && ./demo --script docs/momentum.demo
#  Lines starting with # are comments and are skipped.
#  Press a key to run each command; it types itself and runs.
# ============================================================

# We start on RSA. The prompt bracket always says the current algorithm.
use

# Write a record. Today it's wrapped with RSA.
write Patient MRN-4471, dob 1984-02-11, dx hypertension
read

# Look at the envelope. It names its own algorithm, right in the blob.
show

# The whole move: change the one setting. In a real system it's a config value.
use ML-KEM-768

# New data is post-quantum now. Old data still reads, no migration window.
write Patient MRN-4472, dob 1990-07-30, dx asthma
read
list

# Bring the old record forward. Only the wrap changes; the data is untouched.
rewrap
list

# Policy wants NIST level 5? One word. ML-KEM-1024 is category 5 (~AES-256).
use ML-KEM-1024
write Patient MRN-4473, dob 1975-12-02, dx diabetes
list

# The uncomfortable part: what's actually protecting your data?
cbom

exit
